title: Detour
text: The yellow beam is already on its way to the star. That is the problem.
trick: yellow must be turned away from the starburst it is heading for and brought back diagonally (dual reflector, then quad bender), so the starburst fires straight; its west ray returns to the same dual reflector on the other face, cyan uses it too, and a logic gate takes yellow's straight ray and cyan's bent diagonal ray to make green
motif: open field
proof: not proved; no other solution found in 280 s
expect: merges>=1
